--- SECTION: Trade-offs
[SAY]Let me walk through the key trade-offs. For fault tolerance, we chose SQS with exponential backoff over Kafka — SQS gives us visibility timeouts and dead-letter queues out of the box, less operational overhead than managing Kafka. For deduplication, we went with a Bloom filter over an exact URL store — we traded a small false positive rate for massive memory savings and constant-time lookups at 10 billion scale. And the pipelined architecture adds complexity compared to a monolithic crawler, but it gives us independent scaling and fault isolation per stage.[/SAY]
